A point $a in CC$ is an accumulation point of $X subset.eq CC$ if and only if there exists a sequence $(x_n)$ in $X \\ {a}$ with $x_n -> a$ as $n -> oo$: each threshold $delta > 0$ supplies some $x_n$ with $|x_n - a| < delta$, and the thresholds $delta = 1/n$ build such a sequence; conversely every term $x_n != a$ of a sequence converging to $a$ lies within any given $delta$ of $a$ for $n$ large.
